{
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "praise_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "rationale": "A count of praise statements gives a genuine axis to quantify positivity across reviews, directly supporting the query on praise. Values track the source well (0 for the harshly negative reviews, 4 for the enthusiastic sexploitation review). Minor concern: neutral review IDMB-0005 has some implicit description but scoring 0 is defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "rationale": "Parallel to praise_count and equally useful for measuring negativity intensity. Values are well grounded: 2 complaints for the 'pile of crap' review, 0 for the praise review. Reasonable readings of source text."
    },
    {
      "name": "praised_aspects",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "rationale": "Categorizing WHICH aspects are praised (acting, plot, direction) is exactly the analytical leverage the query asks for. However groundedness is shakier: IMDB-0004 explicitly praises acting ('The acting is pretty good') and visuals/atmosphere, yet the column labels it 'direction' rather than acting, a debatable/partly unsupported mapping. Silent rows correctly NULL/none."
    },
    {
      "name": "complained_aspects",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "rationale": "Aspect-level breakdown of complaints strongly serves the query. Groundedness is mostly sound but inconsistent: IMDB-0001 complains about dialogue/writing ('stilted dialogue', 'insipid writing') and gets 'dialogue|plot', which is reasonable, yet IMDB-0002 and IMDB-0003 register a complaint_count>0 but 'none' aspects despite clear targets (movie quality, wooden performances/acting), suggesting extraction misses. Not hallucinated, but imperfect."
    },
    {
      "name": "review_sentiment_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "rationale": "A four-way praise/complaint/mixed/neutral classification adds a useful grouping axis beyond a bare binary sentiment flag. Mostly grounded, but IMDB-0005 is a clearly critical ('frustrating', 'scumbags') review labeled 'neutral', and IMDB-0001 as 'mixed' is defensible. Somewhat overlaps with the count columns but retains distinct categorical value."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.74,
  "rationale": "The added columns collectively give strong analytical leverage for 'what praise and complaints appear': counts quantify intensity, aspect columns decompose into groupable topics, and the sentiment_type offers a categorical lens. All are non-trivial and non-redundant. Groundedness is generally acceptable with correct NULL handling for silent rows, but several samples show questionable aspect mappings (IMDB-0004 acting-vs-direction) and misses where a count is nonzero yet aspects are 'none', plus a mislabeled 'neutral' on a critical review. No egregious invented facts, so hallucination is limited but reading fidelity is imperfect."
}

